### Phase 2: State Machine Tests
### These tests verify the workflow: DRAFT -> POSTED -> REVERSED

### Prerequisites:
### 1. Create a test user first (if not exists)
### 2. Create a test entity (if not exists)
### 3. Run the database migrations for Phase 2

### ============================================
### STEP 1: Create a DRAFT transaction
### ============================================
POST http://localhost:3000/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "created_by_user_id": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222",
  "type": "RETAIL",
  "currency_code": "KES",
  "transaction_date": "2024-01-29T10:00:00Z",
  "reference": "INV-001",
  "lines": [
    {
      "description": "Nike Shoes",
      "sku": "NIKE-001",
      "quantity": 2,
      "unit_price": 5000,
      "account_code": "200-SALES"
    }
  ]
}

### ============================================
### STEP 2: Post the transaction (DRAFT -> POSTED)
### Replace {transaction_id} with the ID from Step 1
### ============================================
POST http://localhost:3000/transactions/{transaction_id}/post
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222"
}

### ============================================
### STEP 3: Verify transaction is now POSTED
### ============================================
GET http://localhost:3000/transactions/{transaction_id}

### ============================================
### STEP 4: Try to update POSTED transaction (should fail - LOCK 2)
### ============================================
### This should fail with an error about immutability

### ============================================
### STEP 5: Reverse the transaction
### ============================================
POST http://localhost:3000/transactions/{transaction_id}/reverse
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "created_by_user_id": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222",
  "reason": "Customer returned the shoes - wrong size"
}

### ============================================
### STEP 6: Verify reversal was created
### This should show 2 transactions:
### 1. Original with status POSTED
### 2. Reversal with status POSTED and negative amounts
### ============================================
GET http://localhost:3000/transactions?tenant_id=11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

### ============================================
### STEP 7: Export transaction in Universal Invoice format
### ============================================
GET http://localhost:3000/transactions/{transaction_id}/export

### ============================================
### STEP 8: Update payment status to SETTLED
### ============================================
PATCH http://localhost:3000/transactions/{transaction_id}/payment_status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222",
  "status": "SETTLED"
}

### ============================================
### STEP 9: Verify transaction is now RECONCILED
### ============================================
GET http://localhost:3000/transactions/{transaction_id}
